{"shortDescription":"Asia's diesel markets remained upbeat, with margins at a record high and timespreads at five-month highs, while October spot negotiations were underway.October cargoes loading from Northeast Asia continued to be discussed, with two refiners heard to be closing deals in the single-digit premium terr…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia's diesel markets remained upbeat, with margins at a record high and timespreads at five-month highs, while October spot negotiations were underway."]},{"type":"p","children":["October cargoes loading from Northeast Asia continued to be discussed, with two refiners heard to be closing deals in the single-digit premium territory. However, it remains to be seen how spot volumes will compare with September."]},{"type":"p","children":["Talks of run cuts in Northeast Asia were also prevalent, though exact details were still being ironed out."]},{"type":"p","children":["The east-west price spread was little changed at a discount of slightly more than $137 a ton."]},{"type":"p","children":["Refining margins (GO10SGCKMc1) closed the session at a record high of nearly $88 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Cash differentials (GO10-SIN-DIF) inched up to their highest levels since end-July, at around $6.65 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Jet fuel spot discussions were also at premiums for October cargoes."]},{"type":"p","children":["Regrade (JETREG10SGMc1) widened slightly to a discount of more than $4.8 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["SINGAPORE CASH DEALS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- No deal for jet fuel or gasoil."]},{"type":"p","children":["INVENTORIES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- U.S. crude oil, gasoline and distillate stocks all rose last week, market sources said on Tuesday, citing data from the American Petroleum Institute."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Middle distillates stocks held in Fujairah Oil Industry Zone continued hovering at slightly more than 2 million barrels for the week ended September 14, according to industry information service S\u0026P Global Commodity Insights."]},{"type":"p","children":["REFINERY NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Japan's biggest refiner, Eneos Corp, shut the 153,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit at its Negishi refinery near Tokyo on September 7 for scheduled maintenance, a company spokesperson said on Wednesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Saudi Arabia is offering more loadings of crude oil to Asian refiners via ship-to-ship transfer off Oman's Sohar port after drone attacks damaged its key oil pipeline to the Red Sea, people familiar with the matter said."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC) has bought millions of barrels of discounted crude from Iraq's state oil firm, three people familiar with the matter said, expanding its role as a trader amid supply disruptions from the Iran war."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Saudi Arabia has cut oil shipments to Europe after drone attacks damaged its key export pipeline to the Red Sea, trade sources told Reuters, prompting top customers such as Poland to rush to seek alternatives as cargo prices topped $120 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["PRICES"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MIDDLE DISTILLATES"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CASH ($/BBL)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["ASIA CLOSE"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Change"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Prev Close"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":